 <h2 id="strconv"><code>strconv</code></h2>
 <p class="mod-desc">Renders integers as decimal (or base-2/8/16) digit characters into a buffer, and parses them back. Buffers are pankti of integer character codes (not byte-packed strings — see ROUND-08 Part B: Sutram has no byte-write primitive, so we use cell arrays of char codes, the same idiom as lib/baseconv.smlib). All functions handle: zero, negative numbers (decimal only), empty input. int_to_str(n, out) — write decimal representation of int n into pankti out as character codes. Returns the character count (excluding terminator). out[ count ] is set to 0 as a terminator. Caller allocates &gt;= 22 cells.</p>
